R"VG(
# prayer.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the prayer: the call by the faith and the rite, a petition about what has lately
# happened to the place (`@event ... med.pr 3`, prayer_events.vg), the asking in the people's own crops, beasts and roads (the verbs and
# the turns each people's own few: `people=K`), the confession in its own virtues and vices, the giving of its own offerings, the end.
# The lines a reader would remember are each people's own few (`share`), so no two peoples pray the same prayer.

@root med.pr.*

genre.prayer (words=22..100)
  (2) {prayer.call} {prayer.body} {prayer.end}
  (2.5) {prayer.call} {@event fire,storm,pest,flood,drought,sickness,famine,war,battle,quake,eruption,winter,harvest,accident,omen,wonder med.pr 3} {prayer.body} {prayer.end}
  {prayer.call} {med.pr.confess} {prayer.body} {prayer.end}

prayer.call (formula)
  {god.who}, hear us.
  {god}, it is your people at {$home} who ask.
  (faith=ancestors) Old ones, mothers of our mothers, listen.
  (faith=ancestors) You who went before us, turn round a moment and hear us.
  (faith=sky) You who turn {skyone} over us, listen.
  (faith=sky) {god}, behind {skyone}, look down.
  (faith=land) {god}, under our feet, listen.
  (faith=land) {god} of {land}, of the {crop} and of {river}, listen.
  (faith=manygods) {god}, first of the gods, and all of you who listen with {god}, hear us.
  (faith=onegod) {god}, who is one, and alone, and enough, hear us.
  (faith=philosophy) Let us be still, and think, and ask what we may ask.
  (faith=machine) {god}, who counts us, count us kindly.
  (rite=fire) By the fire that has not gone out, {god}, hear us.
  (rite=song) We sing to you, {god}, because you hear singing better.
  In {season.now}, at {holyplace}, we ask.

prayer.body
  {prayer.ask} {prayer.ask} {prayer.give}
  {prayer.ask} {prayer.give} {prayer.ask}
  {prayer.ask} {prayer.ask} {prayer.ask}
  {prayer.give} {prayer.ask} {prayer.ask}

prayer.ask
  (3 once) {med.pr.k} {prayer.what} {prayer.when}.
  (2 once) {med.pr.s} {prayer.for}.
  (2 once) {god}, {med.pr.k.l} {prayer.what} {prayer.when}.
  (2 once) {med.pr.fixed}
  (once sick=1) {med.pr.sick}
  (once famine=1) Fill the {vessel} again; the children are {med.pr.thin}.
  (once war=1) Bring our own home from the war, and the others' too, {med.pr.mothers}; and the {herd} the soldiers took.
  (once harvest<=1) The {crop} was thin last year. Let it be {med.pr.heavy} this year.
  (once stage>=1) {med.pr.late}
  (once desert=1) Send rain, or if not rain, then shade, or if not shade, then {virtue}.
  (once cold=1) Let the {fuel} last until the thaw, and {med.pr.thaw}.
  (0.4 once coast=1) {med.pr.boats}

house.one.n
  {med.house.n}
med.house.n
  (plan=round age<=medieval) round house
  (plan=square age<=medieval) long house
  (plan=court) court house
  (land=stilts) stilt house
  house

med.pr.thaw
  the old ones with it
  the {herd} with it
  the {crop2} in the cellars
  our tempers

med.pr.thin
  thin
  quiet, and that is worse
  eating {med.chr.poor}
  asking why

med.pr.mothers
  if they have mothers
  who also have mothers
  since they were somebody's children first

med.pr.heavy
  heavy
  heavy enough to complain about
  as heavy as the {crop} our mothers talked about
  heavy, and the {pest} elsewhere

med.pr.sick
  Take the sickness away from {$home}; you have taken enough.
  The sick at {$home} are in {med.pr.where}. Sit with them, since we are afraid to.
  Spare the children at {$home} from the sickness, and the old, and then the rest of us.

med.pr.where
  every house
  the hall of {holyplace}
  the long rooms by {town.edge}

med.pr.late
  Do not let us be the last who pray here.
  If you are leaving us, tell us where you are going, and we will follow.
  We are fewer this {season.now}. Count us anyway.
  Keep a place for us, wherever you keep places.

med.pr.boats (share=0.3)
  Bring the boats in, all of them, and the ones in them.
  Bring the boats home over {sea}, low in the water with the catch.
  Keep the boats off the rocks below {$home}, and the boys off the boats.
  Fill the nets with {fish}, and keep the sea out of the boats.
  Calm {sea} for the boats of {$home} until the {fish} are in.
  Let the boats come round the point before dark, and the {bird} with them.
  Keep the {craft} of the nets in the old hands until the young ones learn it.
  Bring the boats back from {sea}; we have enough widows at {$home}.
  Let the {fish} run thick off {$home} and the weather hold until the boats are hauled up.
  Keep the nets whole and the {craft} of mending them in the young hands too.
  Let the boats of {$home} find the {fish} before the boats of {city2} do.
  Send the boats home before {weather}, and the men in them home before the {drink}.

# the verbs, the sendings, the times (each people its own few)
med.pr.k (people=3)
  Keep
  Watch over
  Spare
  Bless
  Remember
  Guard
  Look after
  Hold
  Shelter
  Count
  Mind
med.pr.k.l (people=3)
  keep
  watch over
  spare
  bless
  remember
  guard
  look after
  hold
  shelter
  mind
med.pr.s (people=2)
  Send
  Give us
  Let there be
  Bring
  Grant us
  Do not refuse us

prayer.what
  the {herd}
  the children of {$home}
  the old ones on the hill
  the boats on {river}
  the road to {city2}
  the {crop} in the low field
  {watersrc} and the ones who draw from it
  the ones who are travelling
  the {fruit} on the trees
  the {craft}-house and the hands in it
  the {med.hp} of {$home} and the people under them
  the women who are carrying
  the {veg} in the gardens
  the {herd} and the dogs that keep them
  the {med.chr.trades} at their work
  the {bird} that eat the {pest}
  the bread and the {food} and the hands that make them
prayer.when (share=0.6)
  through {season.next}
  in {weather.now}
  until the harvest
  this year and the next
  as you did for our mothers
  whatever comes
  {time.of}
  until {festival}
  in the dark and in the light
  while we sleep and while we do not
  until the {bird} come back
  until the {crop} is in the {vessel}
  as long as {river} runs

med.hp
  (plan=round age<=medieval) round houses
  (plan=square age<=medieval) long houses
  (plan=court) courts
  (land=stilts) stilt houses
  houses
  roofs

prayer.for
  rain on the {crop} and none on the harvest
  a quiet {season.next}
  {fish} in the nets and none in the cellars
  a good price for the {craft} at {city2}
  sense to the young and patience to the old
  {crop} enough for the {vessel} and some over for the {bird}
  a wind from {dest} when the {crop} is cut
  a short winter and a long memory
  health to the {herd} and to the ones who keep them
  sleep to the ones who have not slept
  {fruit} that ripen before the frost
  a husband for the {med.chr.trades.one}'s daughter, who has waited long enough
  honest weights at the market of {$seat}
  {fuel} enough for the cold nights
  milk from the {herd} and quiet from the neighbours

# the lines a reader remembers: each people its own few
med.pr.fixed (share=0.25)
  Let the children be born alive and outlive us.
  Let the children be born alive and grow tall.
  If the hairy star comes back, let it pass us by.
  Let the {pest} find someone else's {crop}, someone far away who deserves it.
  Let {watersrc} run, and run clean, and run past our door.
  Give the {med.chr.trades} work, and the work honest pay.
  Keep fire from the {roofs} of {$home}.
  Let {moon} come round on time, as you promised.
  (contact=1) Keep the {other} on their side of the river, and us on ours.
  Do not make us rich; make us enough.
  Let the {beast} stop eating the {crop2}, or let us stop minding.
  Keep the roof on the {craft}-house and the rain out of the {vessel}.
  Let nobody die at {festival}; it spoils it for everyone.
  Teach the young ones the songs before the old ones forget them.
  Let the bread rise and the {drink} keep.
  Keep the ones on the road from the ones beside the road.
  Let the {herd} come home by themselves, as they did when we were young.
  Give us one year with nothing in it worth writing down.
  Mend what we broke, and what we will break.
  Let the {bird} wake us, and nothing else.
  Make the stairs of {holyplace} shorter, or our legs longer.
  Keep the {tree} standing; our grandmothers planted them.
  Keep {mountain} where it is.
  Let {river} keep to its bed, as we keep to ours.
  Let the {herd} drop their young in daylight, and the young stand up quickly.
  Keep the {pest} out of the {crop2} and the {med.chr.trades} out of the {drink}.
  Let the {fruit} ripen all together, so the {bird} cannot eat them all.
  Keep the old {tree.n} by {holyplace} standing one more {season.any}.
  Let the {craft} sell at {city2}, and let us not be cheated on the way home.
  Let the new {house.one.n} at {$home} stand longer than the last one.
  Let the {watersrc.n} be clean at {festival}, when everyone comes.
  Keep {mountain} from shaking and {river} from rising and the {herd} from wandering.
  Let the children learn the {craft} before the old hands stop.
  Let the {bird} come back in {season.next} to the same roofs.

prayer.give
  (once) {med.pr.gave}
  (once) We {rite.do} at {holyplace}, as our mothers did.
  (once) We have kept {festival} {med.pr.kept}.
  (once) We ask for {med.pr.only}, nothing more.
  (once) {med.pr.gift.fixed}

med.pr.gave (people=4)
  We have given you {offering}.
  We have hung {colour.holy} cloth at the door, as you like it.
  We have poured {drink} on the threshold, which was not easy this year.
  We have burned {fuel} and {crop} for you, and sat in the smoke.
  We have kept the custom of {feast.custom}, all of us, even the ones who complained.
  We have brought {med.pr.gift} to {holyplace}.
  We have swept {holyplace} and mended the {med.pr.mended}.
  We have left the last of the {crop} in the field for you, and for the {bird}.
  We have cut {motif.over} on the new door, as is right.

med.pr.mended
  roof
  steps
  lamp
  gate

med.pr.kept
  and we will keep it again
  every year, even the hard ones
  as our mothers kept it
  with {feast.custom} and all the rest
  in {colour.holy}, the way you like it
  and burned {fuel} all night for it
  though the {herd} got into the {crop2} while we did
  and nobody fell in {river} this time
  and the {drink} lasted, almost

med.pr.only
  another year
  one more harvest
  a quiet {season.next}
  the {crop} in and the roof on
  rain at night and sun by day
  the {herd} home before {festival}
  {crop2} enough to last the winter
  one {season.any} without a funeral at {$home}
  a fair price for the {craft}
  the {fruit} safe from the {bird}
  a dry floor and a full {vessel.one.n}

med.pr.gift.fixed (share=0.3)
  We have little, and we have given you some of it.
  We have given what we could carry, and the rest we will bring next time.
  It is not much. You have seen our {vessel}.
  We would give more, but you know the year.
  We give you {offering}, and you give us next year. That was the bargain.
  Of the {crop}, the best is yours; the rest is for the {herd}, and us.
  We gave you the {fruit} before we ate any. That was hard; count it.
  The {colour.holy} cloth is new this year. We wove it in {season.now}, in the evenings.
  The {drink} we poured out would have made three of us happy. It is yours.
  The {herd}'s firstborn went to {holyplace} at dawn. It cried all the way.

med.pr.gift
  the first of the {fruit}
  a {vessel.one.n} of {crop2}
  {#n} {coin}
  bread and salt
  a lamb of the {herd}
  a {colour.any} ribbon for every child

# the confession: the people's vices and virtues
med.pr.confess (share=0.8)
  We have been guilty of {vice}; forgive us, and we will try.
  Forgive our {vice}, and keep our {virtue}.
  We have not been {med.pr.good}; we have been {med.pr.bad}, and you saw.
  We forgot you at {festival}. We remembered the {drink}.
  We quarrelled over {watersrc} again. You were there; you heard.
  We were short with the stranger and long with the {drink}.
  We said we would be {med.pr.good} this year. {med.pr.notyet}
  {god}, we are a town of {vice} and good intentions.

med.pr.notyet
  It is {season.now}, and we have not started.
  The {crop} is in, and we have not started.
  We meant it at {festival}. We meant it less by {season.next}.
  We will start after the {herd} are sold.

med.pr.good
  patient
  generous
  honest in the market
  kind to the old
  quiet at the feast

med.pr.bad
  quick to anger
  slow to give
  loud
  greedy with the {crop}
  proud of our {craft}

prayer.end (formula)
  So be it.
  {god.keep}, and us.
  Hear us, and we will not ask again until {season.next}.
  This is the prayer of {$home}, in {season.now}.
  We are done asking. Now we will work.
  Hear this, and do as you think best; you always do.
)VG"
